<title>DENMARK: Danish FLS takes over part of German firm.</title>
<headline>Danish FLS takes over part of German firm.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish cement and engineering group FLS Industries said on Tuesday its environmental unit had taken over the engineering activities of German firm Johannes Mueller and subsidiaries in France and South Africa.</p>
<p>FLS disclosed no price for the acquisition but said Hamburg-based Mueller had 250 staff with an annual turnover of around 250 million crowns.</p>
<p>The Mueller firms manufacture equipment and treatment plants to reduce air pollution in factories in the cement, power and aluminium production sectors, supplementing FLS' own activities, it said.</p>
<p>-- Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
